# resource-generation-flows

## Core Resource Generation Flows
The system implements three distinct resource generation pathways:

1. Case Plan Generation
Path: app/api/generate-plan/stream/route.ts
- Streams real-time case plan resources with 211 database integration
- Prioritizes resources based on urgency classification
- Formats content using trauma-informed care principles

2. Professional Development Resources  
Path: app/api/generate-skill-resource/route.ts
- Generates personalized learning materials from organizational knowledge base
- Adapts content format based on resource type:
  - Worksheets
  - Reading materials
  - Practical exercises
- Incorporates trauma-informed approaches into materials

3. Client-Facing Resources
Path: app/api/generate-client-resource/route.ts
- Creates self-help materials with adaptive complexity
- Applies organizational guidelines and best practices
- Ensures trauma-informed, accessible content formatting

## Knowledge Integration
Path: components/knowledge/BestPracticesManager.tsx
- Manages categorized organizational knowledge for resource generation
- Implements social work domain-specific categorization
- Maintains hierarchical treatment protocol organization

## Resource Generation Rules
- All generated content must incorporate trauma-informed principles
- Professional resources must align with organizational best practices
- Client resources require complexity adaptation based on needs assessment
- Case plans must integrate local resource availability from 211 database

